          "title": "You'll want to know: शर्मिंदा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शर्मिंदा — śarmindā — \"ashamed; embarrassed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अपनी ग़लती पर अरुण शर्मिंदा था। apnī ġaltī par Aruṇ śarmindā thā. Arun was ashamed of his mistake."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शर्मिंदा (śarmindā) is usually traced to Persian sharminda, \"ashamed\", the adjective beside the noun that gave Hindi śarm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
